<p>Kayla,</p>

<p>
This week I am choosing <em>Pornography</em> by The Cure.
</p>

<p>
This is their fourth album, and it’s dark and hauntingly beautiful.
</p>

<p>
I have heard them play all of the songs on this album live at different concerts over the years.
</p>

<p>
My number one favorite, hands down, is “One Hundred Years.”
</p>

<p>
After that, tied for second, are:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Short Term Effect</li>
<li>The Figurehead</li>
<li>A Strange Day</li>
<li>Cold</li>
<li>Pornography</li>
</ul>

<p>
Which leaves “The Hanging Garden” and “Siamese Twins,” and those are really good too.
</p>

<p>
His raw vulnerability, even though I am not part of his experience, draws me in and makes me feel like we are connected.
</p>

<p>
Which is kind of crazy to think about, I know. But when I go to a concert and there are literally thousands and thousands of fans, I can’t help but wonder if they feel just like me. I imagine they do. And that is a powerful gift.
</p>

<p>
Mom
